Native Marker-style document processing in CrispEmbed
===================================================

CrispEmbed's existing original code remains under its MIT license. Native
document-processing files carrying an Apache-2.0 SPDX header and referring to
this notice adapt or are based on the Apache-2.0 Marker implementation. Retain
this notice and models/licenses/apache-2.0/LICENSE when redistributing those
portions or binaries containing them.

Marker, by Vik Paruchuri and Datalab
https://github.com/datalab-to/marker
Revision: 71dd5fd7e51ab24f8624b6ba2fcb6014b4e40ed4 (marker-pdf 2.1.0)

Reference areas include the document/block schema, deterministic document
processors, table reconstruction and Markdown/HTML/JSON renderer contracts.
Changes for CrispEmbed include a new native C++ document representation,
bounded parsing, PDFium integration, conservative text-layout heuristics,
native TeleOCR backend selection, safe output rendering and public interfaces.
This is not the original Python package or the original Surya model pipeline.

TeleOCR inference and its separately licensed model/converter retain the
attributions and terms in NOTICE.teleocr and docs/teleocr-license.md.

The test-only upstream Marker reference uses Apache-2.0 Marker and Surya source,
Apache-2.0 pdftext, and pypdfium2/PDFium. It disables every model-dependent
stage and rejects model calls and network access. Python reference execution
is not a production dependency. No Marker/Surya checkpoint or generated
neural-model output is incorporated in the reference fixtures.

PDFium is an optional, separately supplied native dependency. Redistributors
of a PDFium binary must retain that build's PDFium and third-party licenses.
pypdfium2's test-only binding is Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause; see the selected
distribution's license files. The native runtime does not use that binding.

Marker/Surya source permission does not relicense model weights. Current
Surya 2.5, official GGUF and fast-layout/reading-order checkpoints carry the
modified AI Pubs OpenRAIL-M license. They are not bundled, downloaded, loaded
or required by this implementation. The optional upstream EbookLib/EPUB
dependency is not included. See docs/marker-license.md for exact revisions,
scope, source evidence and unresolved model-license provenance.
